;; x86i's check's classes (bin/repr-asm x86i-check; doc/asm/AMD64.md §10, AX5-DESIGN §4): every row of
;; test/asm/x86i-results-amd64.edn that does not pass is in one of these. In goi's format. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :unimplemented
  :title "an instruction no family claims"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "x86i decodes it (or refuses its encoding: VEX, EVEX, XOP, REX2, 3DNow!) and raises SIGILL, naming it on stderr, never a silent wrong result; the families arrive slice by slice (AX5.4: rcl/rcr, shld/shrd, bit, enter, signal frames; AX5.5: BMI, ADX, SSE/SSE2)"
  :decided "AX5-DESIGN §1, AXS54 (a)"}
 {:id :x87
  :title "x87 instructions"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the x87 file and its instructions are AX6's"
  :decided "AX5-DESIGN §4"}
 {:id :cpuid
  :title "a program that branches on cpuid in a CPU-compared run"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "x86i answers cpuid with its own model (AXS59) and this CPU cannot fault cpuid, so the CPU's run takes another path; the lockstep (AX5.3) overwrites the native answer"
  :decided "AX5-DESIGN §3, AXS58 (a)"}
 {:id :vendor
  :title "a flag or result the SDM leaves undefined and the APM defines"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "x86i does what the APM says; another vendor's CPU differs"
  :decided "AX5-DESIGN §1, AXS55 (a)"}
 {:id :threads
  :title "clone, fork, vfork, execve"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "one thread in AX5: x86i returns -ENOSYS"
  :decided "AX5-DESIGN §1"}
 {:id :nondeterministic
  :title "a program whose output depends on time, randomness or addresses"
  :kind :by-design
  :why "the CPU's run and x86i's differ by the world, not by the machine; the lockstep's world list (AXS58) copies it"
  :decided "AX5-DESIGN §3"}
]
